                                                              "summary":  "Brown pushes back on the Wall Street narrative that AI capex is a bubble, arguing that the current wave of AI applications ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â chatbots, coding assistants ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â is primitive compared to what autonomous agents, humanoid robots, and continuous machine-to-machine communication will demand. He contends that a world with a billion people each running personal AI assistants will require exponentially more compute than currently exists or is being built. The piece frames today\u0027s infrastructure investment not as excess but as foundational underspending relative to the demand curve ahead.",
