                                                              "summary":  "Brown profiles Ron Baron\u0027s decades-long record of conviction investing, highlighting how Baron Capital grew from $10 million to roughly $70 billion in assets through concentrated, long-duration bets on transformative companies. The centerpiece examples are Tesla ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â purchased at $14/share in 2014 ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â and SpaceX, now a $25 billion position, both held through years of market skepticism. Brown frames Baron\u0027s edge not as superior information but as superior patience and the willingness to hold exceptional businesses through turbulence.",
